  codexEntry: 'Quarks are never found alone: they are always bound in groups of three.
    The Nucleon Harvester straddles two quark fields of opposite polarity and draws
    out whole protons (up, up, down) or neutrons (up, down, down), skipping the Combiner
    entirely.'
